[{:db/id "q-141974/selection/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" :answer/id #uuid "1699d48c-fb09-5584-bf02-fb59e39c4f5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141974/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "8f4ba13e-21cc-539e-8498-077deeb957c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141974/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "8e15aa35-000e-57ad-a13f-5431f1957930" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141974/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "e0e0fcc6-a4c0-5bd9-bce9-36959fcdcc35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141974/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "7ee060b1-3746-5e0b-83ad-ec50cd9c83a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141974/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4792ce8e-51ae-5527-b281-d69c7574ea26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141974/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-141974/selection/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" "q-141974/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-141974/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" "q-141974/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-141974/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141974" :question/id #uuid "fc965e10-4874-590e-8c18-9692661389da" :question/math-academy-id "q-141974" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/2b8bbc9ae6b8bf8c441c8e2b534fb159f8180833e1891baa094f988d6a362117.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $D-B?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\frac{6\\pi }{4}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ units up. Hence, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $D-B=1-(\\frac{2}{3})=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141974/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af228cc4-8be2-5c16-8537-4e5dab4e2ff4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141974"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-65448"] :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\pi -(-\\pi )=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n2\\pi =\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{2\\pi }=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Hence, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-143638/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "1479efa3-d543-58b8-bb72-0b25587485c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143638/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "bbdb9508-60e9-581c-850a-2530f82d7c76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143638/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "87ada3ca-84dc-5706-9582-97a08b701b6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143638/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "140de80c-4f26-53f3-a381-356ae8ac989c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143638/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "b9df9813-3fad-5150-a996-c3422f5ef7a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143638/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "18c2557b-a4e9-54c8-b446-9bda2769a428" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143638/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-143638/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-143638/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-143638/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-143638/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-143638/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143638" :question/id #uuid "099318bb-f16c-592c-8396-8642f6dbb6d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-143638" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/112ee04f02087fbf9f477a4cc002a7b24f7881e1ac2e37a1566ccc43e948cf0a.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\pi }=2.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $2$ unit down. Hence, $D=-2.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=2+(-2)=0.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-143638/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af228cc4-8be2-5c16-8537-4e5dab4e2ff4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143638"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "2d6103da-a933-5f3c-8237-e5d132840235" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "92860296-dfb3-5191-91ee-b4a0c5141c29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "119f49a0-bc34-50b8-b276-600854b8e6b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "337dced6-8a5a-546e-b2e9-0a32904fde55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "8b11421c-f405-508e-a3c5-f0e8804caa0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6606a1ed-6024-5de9-8007-316331c1b133" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117796/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer-field/choices ["q-117796/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" "q-117796/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" "q-117796/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-117796/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-117796/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796" :question/id #uuid "5ecbe368-922d-5a9f-956d-5a27886e10df" :question/math-academy-id "q-117796" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/9278723975d70fec73e313d0e164908ddd339231cb74f75b07c2edce14680111.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}-(-\\frac{2\\pi }{5})=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})}=\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{1}{2}$ unit up. Hence, $D=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{4})+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117796/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af228cc4-8be2-5c16-8537-4e5dab4e2ff4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117796"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117795/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "56204d13-e746-5592-8848-2dc92e919d8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117795/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e9802eb8-3fbe-5dec-a5a2-e38dcba2d37c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117795/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "43c95071-cc23-5c59-85e9-6847e9350c15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117795/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "5d9f969d-cf1d-51f1-ab5a-72431daf59ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117795/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "04bcb005-98cd-5cad-b7d8-009b96a173e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117795/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8782fa4-99e0-56ca-9e87-9316a4149688" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117795/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-117795/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-117795/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-117795/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-117795/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-117795/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117795" :question/id #uuid "e52e5ebc-a1b0-593c-b883-50f2676ea209" :question/math-academy-id "q-117795" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/0f920d90aa215300e720ace10bfec9292440d20f32c9b907854b984014f77427.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}=3.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $3$ units down. Hence, $D=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=3+(-3)=0.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117795/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af228cc4-8be2-5c16-8537